# Movie Diary Web App

A simple Flask-based web application to log, filter, and edit your movie-watching history. Users can rate movies, write reviews, mark favorites, and filter their logs by genre, director, year, and more.

## Features

- Add, edit, and delete movie logs
- Filter logs by various criteria
- Track ratings, reviews, and favorites
- Edit shared movie metadata (title, genre, year, etc.)

## Requirements

To run this project, you’ll need to have the following installed:

- Python 3.7+
- `pip` (Python package manager)

**To Install Dependencies**:
pip install -r requirements.txt


## Project Structure
movie-diary/
├── app.py                  # Main Flask app
├── models.py               # SQLAlchemy models
├── templates/              # HTML templates
├── static/
│   └── style.css           # CSS styling
├── requirements.txt        # List of dependencies
└── README.md

## Tech Stack
Python – Core programming language used to build the backend logic.

Flask – Web framework used to create the web application and manage routing, views, and templates.

Flask-SQLAlchemy – ORM (Object-Relational Mapping) tool used for database interactions in an intuitive Pythonic way.

SQLite – File-based relational database used for storing users’ logs and movie information.

Jinja2 – Templating engine (built into Flask) used to render dynamic HTML pages.

HTML/CSS – Frontend technologies used to design the simple, intuitive user interface.